    <table><tr><td>
Listen ye o’brother,
to this grim and bloody tale.
When first we did set forth,
t’was glory and honor we besought.
<br><br>
A proud band of brothers were we.
<br><br>
Many a dragon we did lay low, 
on to victory, our battlecry,
as we sought new foes to slay.
<br><br>
On the fields of battle,
 we new no bounds,
as our enemies lay before us, 
bloodied and broken.
<br><br>
“Tis then that tragedy did strike,
 a fatal blow.
<br><br>
For, in all our greatness,
and all our glory,
sight was lost of true valor,
and in it’s stead, 
venality and arrogance,
did creep in our midst.
Our greatest enemy,
our staunchest foe,
was ourselves.
<br><br>
The final blow,
our brotherhood,
torn asunder and scattered,
amongst the winds.
<br><br>
‘Tis there ye shall find us 
the cries for battle have faded
and the women weep for their dead.
For “Nightmares Asylum” is no more.
